9b06e692 (1861 1793506972563 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f356b") (src . "test: fixture pids found by ps verified before they are signalled\n\nThe census of the fixtures' signal sends left, after the first slice,\n18 sends to pids found by a ps lookup and one rm whose globs carry the\nrun's pid with a `*` right after it. The lookups asked whether a\ncommand line contained `theourgiad.sc serve <store>`, or `serve` and\nthe store anywhere in it, or the subscriber's command and the store as\na substring, so a store whose path begins with this one's (`/x/s`\nagainst `/x/s1`) matched too; and four of them held the pids they found\nand sent to them later, when the process could have ended and its pid\nbeen reused. The globs\n`dmn-*<pid>*` and `.dmn-*<pid>*.lock` match the pid's digits anywhere in\na name, so a run with pid 1234 removes another run's dmn-c51234-x.\n\ntest/signal-send.ss gains the lookup. One listing, `ps -ax -o pid=\n-o lstart= -o command=`, read whole; a lookup answers, for each line\nwhose command text a predicate accepts, the pair of its pid and its\nstart instant from that same listing, and has no side effect, so the\npoll loops and the counts use it as it is (serve-pids, serve-lines).\nserves-store? takes the word after `serve`, or after `serve --store`\n(the client's spelling of a store that begins with `-`), and asks that\nit equal the store, whatever the program's form. A lookup whose\nprocesses are then signalled registers them with the instant read in\nthe listing (register!, started-at!), so a pid that ends and is reused\nbetween the listing and a later `ps -o lstart= -p` is not registered as\nthe newcomer; signal-processes! registers and sends in one call.\npid-identity's answer is trimmed so the two readings of lstart compare\nequal.\n\nThe four identical daemon-pids copies (change-stream-client,\nread-at-cut, unreadable-acknowledge-routes, unreadable-routes) and\nentry-split's daemon-lines and pid-of go; their callers take the\nlookup, and every send to a pid found by ps goes through signal!:\nthe stop-daemon! helpers and term!, entry-split's stops, the lists held\nacross rows (change-stream-client's subscriber, STOPped, CONTed and\nKILLed through the held pairs; f0-ondemand's daemons found by this\nrun's product program, the word before `serve`). change-stream-client\nholds the subscriber alone: the wrapper subshell around it quotes the\nstore in its text and is no longer matched; it writes the rc when the\nsubscriber ends. f0-ondemand's `ps | grep | awk | xargs kill` pipeline\nbecomes the same lookup and signal-processes!. daemon-e1's final rm\nlists the names this fixture builds, each glob with the pid followed by\nthe delimiter the name carries (`-`, `.` or the end), never by `*`.\n\nTests: test/signal-audit.sc grows from 19 to 32 rows. SA-3 gains the\nfive files and changes f0-ondemand's entry (its two ps rows struck),\neleven files in all, their bare sends left named by census row and\nslice (the pid-file sends of the second slice), and requires the lookup\nforms and the checked sends to be present, two or three forms for each\nconverted file here. SA-5, new: no\nremoval glob in test/*.sc has `*` right after a splice of the run's\npid, red on the base with daemon-e1's three. SA-6, new: serves-store?\non eight line forms (`serve /x/s`, `serve /x/s --wire`, `serve --store\n/x/s`, the .so form; not `/x/s1`, `/x/s/`, `--store /x/s1`, a line\nwithout `serve`), and a real `perl -e 'sleep 30' serve <here>/s1` that\nthe lookup for `<here>/s` does not find, the lookup for `<here>/s1`\nfinds with the instant `ps -o lstart= -p` prints for it, and\nsignal-processes! TERM ends. Red first on the base with the new files\nalone: 13 of 32 rows (f0-ondemand's two SA-3 rows, the five converted\nfiles' two each, SA-5). The seven fixtures run alone on the base, on\nthe edit and on a base with the sends' 2>/dev/null dropped print the\nsame rows and lines (f0-ondemand's COST-1 red on all three): no NOTE\nand no \"No such process\", so no pid found by ps ended before its send\nin these runs. Mutants: serves-store? as a substring test\nreds both SA-6 rows; signal! without the instant comparison reds SA-4's\nidentity row and daemon-idle's CONTROL row. The six fixtures of the\nfirst slice that include signal-send.ss keep their rows on the trimmed\npid-identity. Reviewed in one round, no objection from either reviewer.\nrows-baseline.txt takes new hashes for the seven touched fixtures and\nsignal-audit's new hash and counts (32 rows, 51 lines).\n\nStage on an isolated copy of the tree (240 fixtures): only the known\npair red (f0-ondemand COST-1 over its budget, startup-ratio C1/C3);\nthree python fixtures run; row baseline hashes all the described\nversions, the line counts those of the previous stage; no process of\nthe run left; alternation of the compiled product against the base\nmedian 1.0082 (p10 ratios 0.9984, 1.0082, 1.0107), within 1%.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 578))))
